  "docTitle": "Tic-Tac-Toe - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design tic-tac-toe for any board size and any number of players: an O(1) counter-based win check behind a WinStrategy, undo from a move history, and a lock per game, in Java, Python and C++14.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">Read 50 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Build 60 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine coding case</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 20 of the LLD question list</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Tic-Tac-Toe</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">The best first machine-coding problem: small enough to finish in 45 minutes, deep enough for a 60-minute Microsoft or Amazon round. You build an N x N board for any number of players, a win check that costs O(1) per move, a clear game state (in progress, won, draw), undo, and a pluggable win rule for \"4 in a row\" follow-ups. Java, Python and C++14 code all run, and every design choice is explained.</p>\n"
  },
